---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Service | Contractor Ledger';
const description = 'Contractor Ledger terms of use: mathematical estimating guidelines, limitation of liability, and contractor operational responsibility.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 lg:py-14 space-y-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-text-muted" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-text-primary font-semibold">Terms of Service</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-text-primary tracking-tight font-headline">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-text-muted">
        Last updated: October 20, 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-border-default p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-subtle space-y-6 text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          1. Purpose &amp; Nature of Service
        </h2>
        <p>
          Contractor Ledger provides mathematical calculation tools engineered for estimating job pricing, labor burdens, profit margins, break-even thresholds, material procurement markups, and project line items. All calculations are provided free of charge for informational, planning, and verification purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          2. No Legal, Tax, or Engineering Advice
        </h2>
        <p>
          Outputs generated by Contractor Ledger do not constitute legal determinations, certified engineering load models, official accounting filings, or certified payroll compliance under federal (FLSA/Davis-Bacon) or state labor regulations.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Estimating Assumptions:</strong> Factors such as overtime multipliers, employer payroll tax burdens, workers' compensation rates, and scrap waste percentages are user-entered estimating assumptions. Trade contractors and business owners are solely responsible for verifying their own legal wages, statutory tax liabilities, insurance obligations, and client contract commitments.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          3. Limitation of Liability
        </h2>
        <p>
          The calculators use the formulas shown on this site and round currency values to cents. We make no warranties, express or implied, regarding commercial outcomes, winning bids, or actual job profitability. In no event shall Contractor Ledger or its contributors be held liable for bidding errors, cost overruns, operational losses, or contract disputes arising from the use of these tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary font-headline">
          4. Modifications &amp; Continuous Availability
        </h2>
        <p>
          We may update existing formulas or interfaces. Review the calculation methods and assumptions shown with each tool before relying on an estimate.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
